Z||000000||SCFIERO||05-10-2001||09:20 PM||||I am going tomorrow to pick up a 1990 buick lesabre 3800.  It has 60k miles and looks in very good condition.. I am only paying $200 for it.  Can anyone tell me what I need to get out of the rest of the car?  can someone also ell me how many horses as well as can I turn this into a supercharger?  Any info would be great<P>Brian||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric_PA||05-10-2001||09:52 PM||||I got the same year engine from a Lasabre. It's a VIN C rated for 165 HP. I forget off hand what the torque is. I am currently doing a rebuild on it. I am also having a custom balanced flywheel being done by Chris West. As far as what is needed from the car, I didn't do the swap yet so I will learn the hard way. I did however get the wire harness and computer along with all accessories.<P>Here's what it looke like when I got it<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mar20$05.jpg"> <BR>Now it's torn down to the block. The cylinders still had honing marks visible<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Apr23$02.jpg"> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||SCFIERO||05-10-2001||10:33 PM||||Eric,<BR>Can a supercharger be put on this motor?||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCFIERO||05-10-2001||10:59 PM||||ANYONE?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric_PA||05-11-2001||09:30 AM||||I don't know if the supercharger will work on it or not, but I am probably going to use NOS on this engine in the future. I was wondering if you could get the whole intake from a SC 3800 and bolt it on.Now that would be great if it would work.||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||05-11-2001||09:08 PM||||The supercharged engine is quite a bit different.It can't be economically changed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||gabriel||05-12-2001||01:11 PM||||Putting an SC on this engine will prolly cost you more than buying the Seriers II SC, and it will be nowhere near as good as the Series II.  Frankly, I wouldn't do this swap.  The Series II 3800SC is another story ...||||reg||1
